<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<title>QuickSite is installed</title>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  This is a PLACEHOLDER, and it is meant to be deleted.

  QuickSite does not serve anything at the web root on purpose: the root is
  yours, so your own hand-made site can live there and QuickSite never squats
  the domain. On a brand-new install that leaves nothing to serve, and a web
  server with nothing to serve and no directory listing answers 403 Forbidden —
  which looks like a broken install and is not one.

  So setup drops this file in, ONCE, and only when the root had no index file
  of its own. Replace it with your site, or delete it, and nothing changes:
  the root simply goes back to being empty. Nothing in QuickSite reads it.

  It carries meta robots=noindex, but it does still announce that this server
  runs QuickSite. If that matters to you, delete it once you are signed in.

  The link below is deliberately RELATIVE, so it stays correct if the install
  serves from a URL prefix (http://your-domain/web/).
  ============================================================================
-->
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body {
    margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center;
    justify-content: center; padding: 2rem; box-sizing: border-box;
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.6; background: #fafafa; color: #333;
  }
  main { max-width: 34rem; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 .3em; font-size: 1.6rem; color: #1a1a2e; }
  p.sub { margin: 0 0 1.75rem; color: #666; }
  .card {
    background: #fff; border-left: 4px solid #4a9eff; border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin: 1rem 0; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08);
  }
  .card h2 { margin: 0 0 .4em; font-size: 1rem; color: #1a1a2e; }
  .card p { margin: 0; }
  a.btn {
    display: inline-block; margin-top: .5rem; padding: .7rem 1.4rem;
    background: #4a9eff; color: #fff; text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 600;
  }
  a.btn:hover { background: #3d8ae0; }
  code { background: #e8eaf0; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: .9em; }
  footer { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: .85rem; color: #888; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { background: #16161d; color: #cdd6f4; }
    h1, .card h2 { color: #e6e6f0; }
    p.sub, footer { color: #9a9aa8; }
    .card { background: #1e1e2e; box-shadow: none; }
    code { background: #2a2a3c; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>QuickSite is installed</h1>
  <p class="sub">This is the web root, and it is deliberately empty — it belongs to your site, not to QuickSite.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Your admin panel is at <code>/admin/</code></h2>
    <p>On a new installation that page asks you to create the first account, and
       tells you which file on the server holds your setup token.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="admin/">Open the admin panel</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Your sites are at <code>/p/&lt;project&gt;/</code></h2>
    <p>Every project is served from its own folder. A project set to
       <em>private</em> answers 404 to anyone who is not a member — including
       you, until you sign in.</p>
  </div>

  <footer>
    You are seeing this because the web root had no index file when QuickSite
    was set up. Replace this file with your own site, or delete it — nothing
    depends on it.
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
